Description: Add Telit FN920C04 and FN990B40 USB port-type hints.
 ModemManager 1.20.6 predates these modems, so it ships no port-type rules for
 their PIDs (FN920C04 1bc7:10a0/10a2/10a4/10a7/10a9/10aa; FN990B40 1bc7:10d0/
 10d1) and must blind-probe every USB interface to classify it.  That mis-types
 the GPS/QCDM ports ("unhandled port type") and can wedge the modem's command
 stack while it is still booting.  Backport the upstream (ModemManager >= 1.24)
 port-type maps -- GPS / AT primary / AT secondary / QCDM / ignore -- so MM opens
 only the correct ports.  Upstream tags the initial port delay with
 ID_MM_TTY_AT_PROBE_TRIES (added in MM 1.24, not known to 1.20.6), so use the
 1.20.6-era ID_MM_TELIT_PORT_DELAY tag instead.
 The base FN990 (1bc7:1070/1071) already has rules in 1.20.6 and is untouched.
Author: VyOS / iGOS WWAN team
Last-Update: 2026-08-14
Forwarded: not-needed
Origin: backport, https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/mobile-broadband/ModemManager src/plugins/telit/77-mm-telit-port-types.rules

